      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:ab>The ‘Gadla Śamra Krǝstos’ containing the life, the miracles and the image of the saint, is transmitted in only one accessible witness,
              <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr88"><seg corresp="ANLcr88">No item: ANLcr88</seg></t:ref>, which is a 20th-century copy from an older manuscript. According to his gadl, the saint
               monk must have been a contemporary of Metropolitan <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8387SalamaI">Salāmā II</t:persName>, the son of 
               <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10197Yaeqob">Yāʿqob</t:persName> and <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6827Maryams">Maryam Śämrä</t:persName>. He was drawn to his ministry by a
               monk named <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS2665Benyam">Bǝnyām of Dabra Wifāt</t:persName>.</t:ab>
         </t:abstract>
